  "description": "LocateAnything-3B is a 3-billion parameter Transformer-based vision-language model designed for precise object localization, dense detection, and point-based grounding in complex scenes. It utilizes Parallel Box Decoding to predict complete bounding boxes in a single step, achieving up to 2.5× higher throughput than autoregressive approaches while supporting inputs of up to 2.5K images and 24K tokens. The model is built on the MoonViT vision encoder and Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct language model and is released under a non-commercial NVIDIA License for research purposes only.",
